```

The defaults are the ones from the text: a 10-second election timeout and a heartbeat every 2 seconds. The step-down started term 2, and a secondary became primary within the 5 seconds. Here it was mongo2; on your run it may be mongo3, whichever was caught up first. A stepping-down primary asks a caught-up secondary to stand at once, so nobody waits out the 10-second timeout. Once the 20 seconds were over, mongo1 was caught up and had the higher priority, so it called an election, term 3, and won it back. `lastElectionReason` says why: `priorityTakeover`. Each election added one to the term, and no member voted twice in a term.

